  "unreadable": [],
  "uncertain": [
    "Screw terminal: the USB-C connector is only slightly closer to the right (5V) end than the left (GND) end; order from the right end is a near-tie.",
    "SP/CE connector: eight labels (5V, 3V3, CS, SCK, TX, RX, BL, GND) are listed beside the connector; the connector's individual contacts are not distinguishable, so the label-to-contact mapping assumes one label per contact in listed order."
  ],
  "notes": "Callout tokens recorded as printed with their leading peripheral/channel number, e.g. '0 SDA' = I2C0 SDA per the image key (column order SPI/PIO, I2C, UART, PWM, ADC); bare '0','1','2' on GP26-GP28 are the ADC column. Board-tag names (TX, SDA, A0, CS...) placed first in functions; SWC/SWD tags used as functions with callouts SWCLK/SWDIO as labels. Screw terminal GND silkscreen is a ground symbol. Buttons (RESET, BOOT/USER GP22, BTN A GP12) and RGB LED (GP16-18) skipped. Image 2 is the same diagram at lower resolution."
}